      "text": "## Best CRM tools for small consulting firms\n\n**Prices and ratings checked September 5, 2026.** Prices are USD; \u201cannual\u201d means billed annually. Ratings are from Capterra so the comparison uses one consistent review source.\n\n| CRM | Capterra rating | Starting price | Consulting-relevant features | Best fit / main limitation |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| **Less Annoying CRM** | **4.8/5** \u2014 657 reviews | **$15/user/month**, monthly billing | Unlimited contacts and pipelines, tasks, calendar, email logging, custom fields, permissions and 25GB storage/user | **Best simple CRM:** excellent for referral-driven firms and teams of 1\u201320. Limited advanced automation, marketing and project-delivery functionality. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/118921/Less-Annoying-CRM/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Bigin by Zoho CRM** | **4.7/5** \u2014 743 reviews | Free for one user; **$7/user/month annual** for Express | Multiple pipelines, booking pages, web forms, email and WhatsApp integration, built-in phone, workflows, dashboards and Zoho integrations | **Best for solo consultants and micro-firms:** inexpensive and easy to adopt, but reporting and customization may become limiting as the firm grows. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/204998/Bigin-by-Zoho-CRM/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **monday CRM** | **4.7/5** \u2014 466 reviews | **$12/user/month annual**, three-seat minimum | Highly customizable sales and client workflows, email sequences, automations, dashboards, quotes and invoices, communication timelines and hundreds of integrations | **Best customizable sales-to-delivery system:** particularly useful when the firm already uses monday.com. Minimum purchase is effectively **$36/month**, and setup requires more process design. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/245800/Monday-CRM/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **HubSpot CRM / Sales Hub** | **4.5/5** \u2014 4,484 reviews | Free for two users; Starter currently displayed from **$7/seat/month annual**\u2014normally $20 | Contact and deal management, email tracking, meeting scheduling, forms, live chat, templates, basic automation, plus integrated marketing and service tools | **Best for inbound marketing:** strong choice if webinars, content and website leads drive business. Advanced automation becomes expensive\u2014Professional starts around $90/seat/month and requires onboarding. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/152373/HubSpot-CRM/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Pipedrive** | **4.5/5** \u2014 3,058 reviews | **$14/seat/month annual** for Lite; Growth is $39 | Excellent visual pipelines, activity reminders, forecasting and integrations; Growth adds full email sync, tracking, automations, sequences and meeting scheduling | **Best for pure business development:** intuitive for proposal and opportunity tracking. Projects, lead generation and document features may require Premium or add-ons. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/132666/Pipedrive/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Freshsales** | **4.5/5** \u2014 623 reviews | Free for up to three users; **$9/user/month annual** for Growth | Built-in email, phone and chat; contact lifecycle stages, Kanban views, templates, custom fields, workflows, dashboards and AI-assisted features | **Best multichannel value:** useful for firms doing significant outbound prospecting. Advanced scoring, sequences and deal insights require the $39 Pro plan. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/155563/Freshsales/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Capsule CRM** | **4.5/5** \u2014 167 reviews | Free for two users; **$18/user/month annual** for Starter | Contact and pipeline management, tasks, email templates, shared mailbox, accounting integrations, project boards and AI pipeline setup; Growth adds automation and multiple pipelines/project boards | **Best lightweight CRM plus delivery handoff:** particularly well suited to boutique consultancies. For meaningful automation and multiple project boards, expect **$36/user/month** for Growth. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/124041/Capsule/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n| **Zoho CRM** | **4.3/5** \u2014 6,994 reviews | Free edition available; **$14/user/month annual** for Standard | Extensive customization, workflows, dashboards, analytics, email insights, multiple communication channels and close integration with Zoho Books, Projects, Sign and other Zoho applications | **Best feature depth for the price:** suitable for firms with detailed qualification or approval processes. Less intuitive than the simpler CRMs and may need an administrator. ([capterra.com](https://www.capterra.com/p/155928/Zoho-CRM/reviews/?utm_source=openai)) |\n\n## My recommendations\n\n1. **Best overall for a 2\u201315 person boutique: Capsule CRM**  \n   Its combination of relationship management, opportunity pipelines and lightweight project boards maps well to the consulting lifecycle. Consider **Growth at $36/user/month** if you need multiple practice-area pipelines and workflow automation.\n\n2. **Best for a sales-focused consulting firm: Pipedrive**  \n   Choose this if the main problem is inconsistent follow-up, unclear proposal status or poor pipeline forecasting. **Growth at $39/user/month** is the more realistic tier because it includes email synchronization and automation.\n\n3. **Best simple and predictable option: Less Annoying CRM**  \n   A strong choice when partners primarily win work through referrals and need one place for contacts, notes, opportunities and follow-up tasks\u2014not a large marketing platform.\n\n4. **Best for marketing-led firms: HubSpot**  \n   Ideal if content, newsletters, webinars and website forms are important acquisition channels. Carefully model the cost of Professional features, marketing contacts, AI credits and onboarding before committing.\n\n5. **Best for solo consultants or teams under five: Bigin**  \n   It offers unusually strong pipeline, scheduling and communication functionality for $7 per user. Firms can later migrate into the broader Zoho ecosystem.\n\n6. **Best for connecting sales with client delivery: monday CRM**  \n   Its flexibility makes it useful for tracking opportunities, onboarding, engagements and renewals in related workflows. It works best when someone is willing to design and maintain the boards and automations.\n\n### Important purchasing note\n\nMost of these are primarily **sales CRMs**, not full professional-services automation systems. If you also need resource allocation, utilization, time tracking, engagement profitability or detailed billing, verify integration with your project-management and accounting stack\u2014or consider a consulting-focused PSA alongside the CRM. Ratings should also be weighed by sample size: a 4.5 based on thousands of reviews is stronger evidence than the same score based on fewer than 200."
     }
