      ],
      "logprobs": [],
      "text": "**For a two-person consulting firm, I\u2019d choose Capsule CRM.**\n\n### Why Capsule\n\n- **The free plan covers exactly two users**, so both partners can use it without paying.\n- It supports the full basic consulting lifecycle: **contacts \u2192 opportunities \u2192 won engagements \u2192 project tasks**.\n- You can store notes and emails against each client, assign follow-ups and track proposals in a visual pipeline.\n- Its project view can manage lightweight deliverables, deadlines and responsibilities\u2014something simpler CRMs often lack.\n- It\u2019s easier to configure and maintain than HubSpot, Zoho or monday CRM, which matters when neither partner wants to become the CRM administrator.\n\nThe free plan allows **250 contacts, one sales pipeline and one project board**. That is enough to validate whether the system fits your workflow before upgrading. ([capsulecrm.com](https://capsulecrm.com/signup/?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Suggested setup\n\nCreate pipeline stages such as:\n\n1. New lead  \n2. Discovery scheduled  \n3. Qualified opportunity  \n4. Proposal being prepared  \n5. Proposal submitted  \n6. Verbal commitment  \n7. Won/lost  \n\nAfter winning an engagement, move it to the project board with milestones such as kickoff, information gathering, analysis, draft deliverable, client review and completion.\n\n### When I\u2019d choose something else\n\n- **Less Annoying CRM:** if you only need contacts, deals and reminders\u2014not project tracking.\n- **Pipedrive:** if you have a substantial volume of prospects and rigorous business-development activity.\n- **HubSpot:** if website forms, newsletters and inbound marketing are central to growth.\n- **Bigin:** if automation and integrations matter more than project management. Its free plan supports only one user, so a two-person firm would need Express at **$7 per user per month billed annually**. ([bigin.com](https://www.bigin.com/articles/faqs-about-bigin.html?utm_source=openai))\n\n**Bottom line:** Start with Capsule\u2019s free plan. Upgrade only when you exceed 250 contacts or need multiple pipelines, accounting integrations or more advanced automation."
